What:           /sys/class/remoteproc/remoteproc*/crash_count
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Uke Linux contributors
Description:
                Read-only unsigned decimal count of crashes handled for this
                registered remote processor, followed by a newline. The count
                is retained across automatic firmware recovery and ordinary
                stop/start. It is reset when the remoteproc object is recreated
                and follows the existing unsigned 32-bit counter's wraparound.

                Reading this attribute does not query firmware, start a remote
                processor, change recovery policy or wait for a DSP operation.
                It is a snapshot, not an atomic snapshot of state and count.

                Event consumers should subscribe to remoteproc notifications
                before reading the initial count. The existing crash change
                event remains the event source; this attribute has no timer,
                acknowledgement, writable reset or independent poll protocol.
                A missing attribute on an older kernel means history is unknown,
                rather than proving that no crash occurred.
